  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "27",
  "quote": "(1) A landlord may enter a rental unit in accordance with written notice given to the tenant at least 24 hours before the time of entry under the following circumstances:",
  "reason": "Under sections 25 and 27, a landlord may only enter a rental unit to carry out an inspection if they provide written notice at least 24 hours in advance. Because this clause purports to allow the landlord to enter for routine inspections without arranging it in advance and without notice or consent at the time of entry, it conflicts with the Act and is void under section 4(1)."
}

